{
  "_comment": [
    "Ontology table for the demo machine's generated knowledge graph.",
    "",
    "'family_to_class' maps every FAMILY token of the control_assistant tier-3 channel",
    "database to a class in the NARAD shared-semantics vocabulary; 'classes' declares",
    "those classes and their rdfs:subClassOf parents, closed up to the root",
    "'AcceleratorDevice'.  The hierarchy is copied edge-for-edge from the NARAD",
    "shared-semantics vocabulary the als-ontology project defines, so a class-rollup",
    "query written against any NARAD graph returns the analogous answer on the demo graph.",
    "",
    "Every class name here exists in that vocabulary, and each one's skos:altLabel",
    "list is the vocabulary's list verbatim.  Three classes carry additional demo-only",
    "synonyms, because the demo machine names devices the vocabulary has no word for:",
    "  - BeamCurrentMonitor gains 'dcct' (the demo's DCCT family).",
    "  - BeamLossMonitor gains 'gamma monitor', 'neutron monitor', 'radiation monitor'.",
    "  - Modulator gains 'klystron', 'modulator', 'rf modulator'.",
    "",
    "APPROXIMATION: the demo machine's GAMMA and NEUTRON families are radiation",
    "monitors, and the NARAD vocabulary has no radiation-monitor class.  Both map to",
    "BeamLossMonitor, the nearest existing class -- a diagnostic that counts particles",
    "lost from the beam.  This is deliberate: the demo corpus stays inside the shipped",
    "vocabulary rather than inventing a class the ALS graph would not recognise.  A",
    "facility whose real ontology has a better class should ship its own table.",
    "",
    "The CAVITY family maps to AcceleratingCavity rather than to one of its subclasses",
    "(NormalConducting / Superconducting), because the demo machine's channel database",
    "does not say which technology the cavities use."
  ],
  "root": "AcceleratorDevice",
  "family_to_class": {
    "BPM": "BeamPositionMonitor",
    "CAVITY": "AcceleratingCavity",
    "DCCT": "BeamCurrentMonitor",
